    "https://utwentecareers.nl/en/contact/": {
      "title": "Getstartedwith research and educationthat matter",
      "description": "Contact | University of Twente Vacancies Academic staff Support staff UT Student Jobs UT as employer UT as employer Employment conditions Career and development Pre and onboarding Tenure Track PhD EngD Working as a UT student Stories from UT employees Job alert About UT Campus Research institutes Strategy and culture Twente and Enschede Nederlands English en Nederlands English contact Get started with research and education that matter Making an impact in our society starts with a first acquaintance. Contactgegevens Universiteit Twente DRIENERLOLAAN 5 7522NB ENSCHEDE +31(0)53 489 9111 info@utwente.nl Wil je nog meer leren over Universiteit Twente? Vraag het onze chatbot! Of heb je een vraag over een vacature? Bel of mail dan naar de contactpersoon die in de vacaturetekst staat. Route en plattegrond University of Twente Drienerlolaan 5 7522NB Enschede +31(0)53 489 9111 info@utwente.nl Route Quicklinks Scientific Staff Support Staff Contact Follow us LinkedIn Twitter RSS Cookies & Privacy Stay informed. After registration you will regularly receive our new vacancies. Subscribe as External applicant UT Employee (will receive internal vacancies) Email address Login Occupation Administrative & facility Assistant professor Associate professor Education EngD Finance HRM IT Lecturer Legal staff Management Marketing and communications PhD Policy and staff PostDoc Professor Research, development, innovation Researcher Technical and laboratory You are signed up for the Job alert Previous Next Sign up Cookies We use cookies and similar technologies to process your personal data (e.g. IP address) for personalised content, ads and third-party media integrations. Functional and strictly analytical cookies are always set. Non-essential and non-analytical cookies require your permission. For more details, see our privacy statement or cookie policy . Reject Accept"
    },
    "https://twitter.com/utwentejobs": {
      "title": "",
      "description": ""
    },
    "https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/rss/": {
      "title": "",
      "description": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" ?>\n<rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/\">\n  <channel rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/\">\n    <title>Vacancies at the University of Twente</title>\n    <description>Working at the University of Twente. Good choice! There is plenty of space at the University of Twente. There&#38;apos;s space for ambition, and space for talent. Space for your own ideas and using your initiative. At Twente, we will value and encourage your entrepreneurial spirit. We can offer you great career prospects and ambitious, discerning colleagues. We will provide plenty of training and courses to develop your skills. And of course, we can offer a good salary and excellent fringe benefits.</description>\n    <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/</link>\n    <image rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/.publisher/sd/utwente_jobs/utvacancies/img/icons/favicon.ico\" />\n    <dc:language>en</dc:language>\n    <dc:date>2026-09-03T17:39:21+00:00</dc:date>\n    <items>\n      <rdf:Seq>\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2589\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2588\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2583\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2581\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2566\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2567\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2550\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2537\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2419\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2341\" />\n        <rdf:li rdf:resource=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#873\" />\n        \n      </rdf:Seq>\n    </items>\n  </channel>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2589\">\n      <title>SCIENTIFIC DIRECTOR Digital Society Institute DSI</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2589/scientific-director-digital-society-institute-dsi/</link>\n      <description>The Scientific Director embraces an inspiring and supportive leadership style and heads the Management Team that collectively leads the DSI institute. You will represent the UT in setting the research agenda, promoting the institute and the university, creating and maintaining regional, national an&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 22:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2588\">\n      <title>Two Postdoc positions for max. 2.5 years in Photonics for Quantum</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2588/two-postdoc-positions-for-max.-2.5-years-in-photonics-for-quantum/</link>\n      <description>Your home base will be the Adaptive Quantum Optics (AQO) chair at the MESA+ Institute for Nanotechnology, University of Twente. Within P4Q, you will work on photonic integrated circuits (PICs) for quantum communication and quantum networking. A central element of the project is the integration of h&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 22:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2583\">\n      <title>Assistant/Associate Professor in Power Electronics</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2583/assistantassociate-professor-in-power-electronics/</link>\n      <description>The Power Electronics Group at the University of Twente is seeking an outstanding Assistant or Associate Professor to strengthen its internationally recognised research and education activities in modern power electronic systems. You will develop an independent research line that complements and st&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2581\">\n      <title>PhD-position Towards the next generation of tires: Development of micro-abrasive resistant tire treads</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2581/phd-position-towards-the-next-generation-of-tires-development-of-micro-abrasive-resistant-tire-treads/</link>\n      <description>Car tires are very important and complex parts with high safety and reliability requirements, responsible for maintaining the contact between a vehicle and the road. Tires are subject to wear due to the tire &#8211; road interaction, causing the emission of micro particles in the environment with polluti&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 22:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2566\">\n      <title>PhD position on flexible structural causal modelling in extreme value statistics</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2566/phd-position-on-flexible-structural-causal-modelling-in-extreme-value-statistics/</link>\n      <description>In this project, we develop a new mathematical framework to efficiently model multivariate systems during extreme events like floods, heatwaves, or financial crashes. This PhD position offers a combination of theoretical research and the implementation of new statistical methodology and thus requir&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 22:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2567\">\n      <title>EngD on AI-robotic integration for arm assistance in home settings</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2567/engd-on-ai-robotic-integration-for-arm-assistance-in-home-settings/</link>\n      <description>SAISaAR-bot. Supporting AI-based system for autonomous use of the iFLOAT robotic arm for assistance and rehabilitation in home settings. SAISaAR-bot, is a Vanguard Vinnovate project that builds collaboration between two European Regions (East Netherlands, The Netherlands, and Emilia-Romagna, Italy)&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 22:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2550\">\n      <title>Researcher in Semantic Interoperability and Explainable, Knowledge-driven AI for Smart Systems (SAREF4XAI)</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2550/researcher-in-semantic-interoperability-and-explainable-knowledge-driven-ai-for-smart-systems-saref4xai/</link>\n      <description>The rising popularity of AI-powered smart environments for building automation and management raises concerns about interoperability, transparency, and trust. These environments often operate across heterogeneous domains, rely on various standards and protocols, and are tailored to different tasks.&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 22:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2537\">\n      <title>Postdoc position on microfluidic mass production of therapeutic microgels</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2537/postdoc-position-on-microfluidic-mass-production-of-therapeutic-microgels/</link>\n      <description>Are you passionate about combining microfluidic technology, material science, device engineering, and cell therapeutic strategies towards real-world applications ? We offer an impactful postdoc position in the Leijten Laboratory within the Department of BioEngineering Technologies as part of a rece&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Sun, 28 Jun 2026 22:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2419\">\n      <title>Hockeytrainer/coach DHC Men 1 &#38; 2</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2419/hockeytrainercoach-dhc-men-1-2/</link>\n      <description>Feeling with student sports  Student life, study pressure, exams and internships can have an impact on the performance and presence of players and team. The new trainer/coach is expected to be able to deal with this well. In addition, training courses can be offered by you (partially) in English if&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Mon, 16 Mar 2026 23:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#2341\">\n      <title>Research Technician in Molecules &#38; Materials</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2341/research-technician-in-molecules-materials/</link>\n      <description>The Research Technician will be involved in current research topics, which include activities such as, among others, the synthesis of new building blocks for self-assemblies, molecules for surface functionalization and nanoscale and organic materials; analysis of such materials. The technician will&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Tue, 06 Jan 2026 23:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  <item rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/#873\">\n      <title>PhD position in IC Design group</title>\n      <link>https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/873/phd-position-in-ic-design-group/</link>\n      <description>The University of Twente (UT) is located in the east of the Netherlands. It offers a dynamic campus, excellent facilities and the possibility to work in- and with- famous research groups. Professor Bram Nauta&#8217;s Integrated Circuit Design (ICD) group focuses on various aspects of analog and Radio Fre&#8230;</description>\n      <dc:date>Thu, 27 Oct 2022 22:00:00 GMT</dc:date>\n    </item>\n  \n  <image rdf:about=\"https://utwentecareers.nl/.publisher/sd/utwente_jobs/utvacancies/img/icons/favicon.ico\">\n    <title>University of Twente.</title>\n    <link>https://www.utwente.nl/</link>\n    <url>https://utwentecareers.nl/.publisher/sd/utwente_jobs/utvacancies/img/icons/favicon.ico</url>\n  </image>\n</rdf:RDF>"
    },
    "https://utwentecareers.nl/en/cookies/": {
      "title": "Wat is eencookie?",
      "description": "Cookies | University of Twente Vacancies Academic staff Support staff UT Student Jobs UT as employer UT as employer Employment conditions Career and development Pre and onboarding Tenure Track PhD EngD Working as a UT student Stories from UT employees Job alert About UT Campus Research institutes Strategy and culture Twente and Enschede Nederlands English en Nederlands English cookies Wat is een cookie ? A cookie is a simple small file that is sent along with pages from this website and/or other web-based applications and is stored on your device by your browser. The information stored therein can be sent back to our servers on a subsequent visit. These cookies do not collect any personal information and do not damage your computer. Allow third party cookies Your choice will be saved automatically. Use the back button to go back to the page you came from. The cookie notification will disappear automatically. THE UNIVERSITY OF TWENTE WEBSITES USE THE FOLLOWING COOKIES: Functional and technical cookies: Permanent cookies Session cookies Cookie control cookies Analytics cookies: Google Analytics (analytische cookies) Usabilla feedback Monsido website improvement Messagebird chat Advertising and marketing cookies: Remarketing cookies Advertising programmes Social Media-cookies: Cookies for commenting on articles and sharing pages Viewing YouTube or Vimeo video’s and other embedded content FUNCTIONAL AND TECHNICAL COOKIES (COOKIES THAT ARE STRICTLY NECESSARY) Technical cookies are cookies needed for the proper performance of our websites, such as language preference, to be able to login or to detect fraud with your account. Functional cookies remember your preferences. This includes making it possible to retrieve submitted personal data for some event registrations out of the database, or to remain logged in during a browsing session. Please note that we only use these cookies to guarantee a user-friendly visit and a proper website performance. THE USE OF PERMANENT COOKIES By means of permanent cookies, the website identifies you during a visit to apply your settings or identify you as a new user. The cookie stores a unique random identifier to recognise you. This cookie is essential to ensure that all website functionality is available to you, making website usage more convenient. You can remove permanent cookies through the settings feature of your browser. THE USE OF SESSION COOKIES During a session, the website stores status updates and preferences. This enables us to adapt our services to the behaviour of our visitors and to make the website as easy to use as possible. This website uses for example session cookies that keep you logged in while surfing on our website, remember search queries, etc. These cookies will be automatically deleted when you close your web browser. COOKIE CONTROL COOKIES These cookies are stored on your computer to remember your preferences with regard to the use of cookies. These are necessary to know if you agree or do not agree to the use of specific cookies. You can change these settings above this text. ANALYTIC COOKIES GOOGLE ANALYTICS This website uses Google Analytics, a web analytics service provided by Google, Inc. Google Analytics sets cookies in order to evaluate your use of the website and compile reports for us on activity on the site. Google can provide this information to third parties when Google is legally forced to do so, or to the extent that third parties process data. We do not have influence on this process. We have closed a processing agreement with Google Analytics, imposing legal boundaries on the data processing within the European Economic Area (EEA). We did not allow Google to use the analytics data for other services provided. The information collected by Google Analytics is anonymised as much as possible. The last identifier of your IP-address is explicitly not collected. The information is transferred trough a secure connection (SSL) and stored by Google on servers across the globe. Google Inc. and all its subsidiaries, including Google Analytics, adhere to the EU-US Privacy Shield Framework. Read more about Google’s Privacy Policy . ADVERTISING AND MARKETING COOKIES THIRD PARTY COOKIES Other parties will place “tracking cookies” in your browser to match ads to your preferences. These cookies will remember the pages you visited apart from their network, to create a profile of your online behaviour. This profile will be created, using similar information of your visits to other websites in the third party’s network. This profile does not store any personal information, such as your name and email address, as known to us. Its only purpose is to match advertisement to your profile, which makes them as relevant and interesting to you as possible. ADVERTISING COOKIES Google, Facebook and other advertising platforms use cookies to show relevant ads based on your recent queries and site visits, based on your recent search queries. Some promotional sections on the University of Twente websites use cookies from Google, Facebook and other platforms to register user interactions on the website. REMARKETING COOKIES Some promotional sections on the University of Twente websites use cookies for remarketing via Google, Facebook or other advertising platforms. This means that ads can be shown on Facebook, websites in the Google Display Network and other networks that match your preference, based on your website visit. SOCIAL MEDIA SHARE BUTTONS This website has buttons and icons to promote or share web pages (to “like” or “tweet”). These buttons only work, when using scripts and codes that are generated by networks like Facebook and Twitter.  This code generates cookies when actively used by Add This, when interacting with the buttons. We do not have any influence on this. Please read Facebook, Twitter’s or other network’s privacy statement (which can change often) to read what they use your personal details for by using these cookies. The information the cookies collect is stored anonymously. The information is sent by and to Twitter, Facebook and others, possibly on servers situated in the US. Facebook, Twitter and Google have committed to the  EU-US Privacy Shield to comply to European standards for handling personal information. YOUTUBE AND VIMEO VIDEOS, EMBEDDED CONTENT In order to be able to watch the YouTube, Vimeo and other embedded content on the websites, YouTube will set cookies. Read YouTube or Vimeo privacy policy to see how they process the data they collect. REJECTING OR DELETING COOKIES Would you like to reject or accept cookies, or change your settings? You can do this through our cookie settings above this text or through the settings feature of your browser, e.g. Chrome, Edge, Internet Explorer, Safari, Firefox, Mozilla or Opera. More information about changing your cookie settings or deleting cookies can be found in the browser setting, or by using the help option of your browser. These are different for each browser. You can choose to enable the “do-not-track”-feature. DELETING AND ACCEPTING TRACKING COOKIES BY THIRD-PARTIES: Some tracking cookies are set by third-parties to show ads (through our website and other websites) that match your preferences. These cookies can be removed in a central location through Your Online Choices , which ensures the fact that they will not be set on any other website. It is possible to determine through your browser settings (Chrome, Edge, Internet Explorer, Safari, Firefox, Mozilla or Opera) if and what type of cookies you accept. Where to find these settings, is different for each browser. Please use the help feature of your browser to find the exact location and method. REJECTING SPECIFIC COOKIES: If you reject certain cookies, the website’s good performance may not be guaranteed. Rejecting cookies, does not mean that you will not see any advertisements anymore. However, the ads may not be tailored to your preferences anymore. MORE INFORMATION ABOUT COOKIES Please do not hesitate to contact us for more information. We would also like to refer to our Privacy Statemen t for general privacy information. University of Twente Drienerlolaan 5 7522NB Enschede +31(0)53 489 9111 info@utwente.nl Route Quicklinks Scientific Staff Support Staff Contact Follow us LinkedIn Twitter RSS Cookies & Privacy Stay informed. After registration you will regularly receive our new vacancies. Subscribe as External applicant UT Employee (will receive internal vacancies) Email address Login Occupation Administrative & facility Assistant professor Associate professor Education EngD Finance HRM IT Lecturer Legal staff Management Marketing and communications PhD Policy and staff PostDoc Professor Research, development, innovation Researcher Technical and laboratory You are signed up for the Job alert Previous Next Sign up Cookies We use cookies and similar technologies to process your personal data (e.g. IP address) for personalised content, ads and third-party media integrations. Functional and strictly analytical cookies are always set. Non-essential and non-analytical cookies require your permission. For more details, see our privacy statement or cookie policy . Reject Accept"
    },
